{"author": "ValWood", "body": "\nRe\nWould GO:0000001 mitochondrion inheritance be the alternative choice here?\n\nThis is also a bit of a weird term, but it is more about partitioning of the mitochondria at cell division. The part  about DNA in the definition is misleading  because that seems to be more of a consequence... \nI think we also need to review how this term relates to fission and fusion, but this is broader because it would include movement of mitochondrial by cytoskeletal processes... \nI think inheritance is largely stochastic ,  but not in budding yeast  where actin is involved so there are clearly organism specific differences (and still emerging).\n\n\n\n", "created_at": "2025-04-29T15:07:48Z", "key": "comment:2839278884", "type": "comment", "updated_at": "2025-04-29T15:07:48Z"}
